From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 07:49:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] mfsensorgroup: Add the DLL, with a sensor activity monitor.

PowerPoint delay-loads MFCreateSensorActivityMonitor from
mfsensorgroup.dll during a slide show, some twenty seconds into it here
after the pointer had been used.  Wine had no such DLL: the delay load
raised 0xc06d007e, nothing caught it, and PowerPoint died in the middle
of the show.

The monitor is how Windows tells an application which processes stream
from which camera, as its frame server learns it.  Wine has no frame
server and does not know, so the report a monitor gives after Start, on
a thread of the pool, holds no sensors.  Stop ends the reports and a
new Start reports again; a report under way when the monitor goes still
reaches the callback, which the monitor holds until then.  PowerPoint
now creates one, starts it on another thread, reads the empty report
and goes on with the show.

The five interfaces are declared in mfidl.idl with the Windows SDK's
IIDs; IMFSensorActivitiesReportCallback's is also in ppcore.dll.

Not measured yet: E_POINTER for either NULL argument, E_INVALIDARG for a
report index out of range and MF_E_NOT_FOUND for an unknown device name,
whether Windows reports at once after Start, and repeated Start and
Stop.  tools/sensoractivityprobe in the outer tree asks Windows.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

